      "main": ["Belfast never had a scene.", "He made one anyway."],
      "sub": "Calibre and the art of staying outside."
    },
    {
      "type": "body",
      "text": [
        "Age 5.",
        "Selected from 400 pupils",
        "for classical violin training",
        "at the Belfast School of Music.",
        "He also played tin whistle",
        "in traditional Irish bands.",
        "Outside, the city was burning.",
        "Music was somewhere else."
      ],
      "sub": "Belfast. The Troubles. 1970s–80s."
    },
    {
      "type": "body",
      "text": [
        "His brother played him jungle",
        "in the early '90s.",
        "It didn't click.",
        "Then one day it did.",
        "He started producing drum and bass in 1995.",
        "Inspired by Goldie. Inspired by LTJ Bukem.",
        "The first exclusively Irish DnB artist."
      ],
      "sub": "Northern Ireland enters the continuum."
    },
    {
      "type": "body",
      "text": [
        "His first album, Musique Concrète,",
        "came out in 2001.",
        "On Creative Source — Fabio's label.",
        "Not London. Not a major.",
        "Fabio believed in him",
        "before most people had heard his name."
      ],
      "sub": "Debut. 2001. Creative Source."
    },
    {
      "type": "body",
      "text": [
        "He founded Signature Recordings.",
        "He has released every major album himself.",
        "No A&R.",
        "No label telling him what to cut.",
        "No compromise.",
        "Just music",
        "and time."
      ],
      "sub": "Signature Recordings, est. 2003."
    },
    {
      "type": "body",
      "text": [
        "Second Sun. 2005.",
        "Still considered a milestone",
        "in liquid drum and bass.",
        "Remastered. Re-released in 2019.",
        "Some records don't age.",
        "They deepen."
      ],
      "sub": "A record that only gets deeper."
    },
    {
      "type": "body",
      "text": [
        "The Shelflife series.",
        "8 volumes.",
        "Music that didn't make the albums.",
        "He put it out anyway.",
        "Vinyl. Proper releases.",
        "Because every track counted."
      ],
      "sub": "The archive as philosophy."
    },
    {
      "type": "cta",
      "text": [
        "\"Any type of instrument I could get my hands on,",
        "I'd record it live.",
        "It helped create my own sound.\"",
        "— Dominick Martin, Calibre"
      ],
      "strobe": "30 years. No compromise.",
      "cta": "Save this."
